    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the **salutation** feature: `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), which is stored and reflected back on `GET /api/owners/{id}` as a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the project's existing conventions for derived owner fields (like `contactPreference`, `displayName`), I put each piece where it belongs:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (input) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `salutation` (`readOnly`, derived) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the stored `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so it round-trips through persistence. MapStruct maps `title` DTO\u2194entity automatically by name.\n\n3. **`util/Salutation.java`** \u2014 a new single-responsibility helper (mirroring `ContactPreference` et al.) that composes the salutation from an `Owner`.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `salutation` via `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(salutation(owner))\")` delegating to `Salutation.of`, exactly like the other derived read-only fields.\n\n5. **DB schema** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run under hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the script).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
